**Story & Context:** At 127 BPM, Awa opens with a two-note bolon figure whose first STRIKE produces a strong calabash BLOOM and whose second dies quickly. Leon builds a swung kick pattern around it but intentionally removes the expected third subdivision of each two-bar phrase. Mariam answers that absence with one deadened clavinet fourth only every second cycle. Boubacar replaces one programmed tom with a low palm strike on calabash. Elliot stays silent until bar sixteen, then adds one breath-led bass-flugelhorn fifth after a long POCKET. The central section keeps the same bolon figure while the location of the Empty Third shifts by one sixteenth note, making the groove feel displaced without changing tempo or harmony.

