## 3. Last Departure Waits Inside the Pocket

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 124 BPM and begins with almost no synthetic low end. Awa plays widely spaced bolon plucks with long POCKET windows. Leon uses only kick, shaker, and occasional displaced clap. Mariam places one muted clavinet octave every four bars. Boubacar answers alternate bolon RETURNS with soft calabash heel strokes. Elliot sustains one low brass note only at major section changes. In the final minute, Awa progressively shortens BLOOM by muting the calabash body sooner while Leon delays the sub further and further into POCKET. On the final phrase, the bolon STRIKE and BLOOM end completely; the band waits almost a full beat before one short sine-sub note confirms the last RETURN, then stops dry.

